CAT = "sqeLand"; SEG = "LAN"
Q = [
("A five-year lease is granted in signed writing but not by deed. What does the tenant hold?",
 "Equitable lease", ["Legal lease", "Bare licence", "Nothing at all in law"],
 "A lease over three years must be made by deed to be legal (s.52 LPA 1925). A written lease satisfying s.2 LP(MP)A 1989 can take effect as an equitable lease under Walsh v Lonsdale."),
("A written contract to sell land is signed by the buyer but not by the seller. Is it binding?",
 "No, both must sign", ["Yes, the buyer signed", "Yes, if exchanged", "Only if witnessed"],
 "Section 2 LP(MP)A 1989 requires a contract for the sale of land to be in writing, contain all agreed terms and be signed by or for each party."),
("A wife with an equitable share lives in a house registered to her husband alone. He sells to one buyer. Her interest?",
 "It overrides", ["Lost once the sale registers", "Binds only if noticed", "Converted into money"],
 "An interest of a person in actual occupation overrides a registered disposition under Sch 3 para 2 LRA 2002, unless it is overreached or she failed to disclose it when asked."),
("A buyer pays the price to two trustees of land. What happens to the beneficiaries' interests?",
 "They are overreached", ["They bind the buyer", "They are extinguished", "They need court approval"],
 "Payment of capital money to at least two trustees overreaches beneficial interests (ss.2 and 27 LPA 1925): they move into the proceeds of sale."),
("A joint tenant wants to sever the beneficial joint tenancy. Which step alone is enough?",
 "Written notice to him", ["Telling a friend orally", "Making a new will", "Moving out of the house"],
 "Section 36(2) LPA 1925 allows severance by written notice given to the other joint tenants. A will cannot sever, and moving out does not."),
("Which unity is needed for a tenancy in common?",
 "Possession", ["Title", "Interest", "Time and title"],
 "A tenancy in common needs only unity of possession; a joint tenancy needs all four unities of possession, interest, title and time."),
("Co-owners of a home disagree about selling it. What can one of them do?",
 "Apply to court for an order", ["Serve a notice to quit", "Apply to rectify the register", "Sell the whole house alone"],
 "Under s.14 TOLATA 1996 a co-owner can apply for an order, including an order for sale; the court considers the s.15 factors such as the purposes of the trust."),
("Which is essential for a right to exist as an easement?",
 "Dominant and servient land", ["A payment for the right", "Registration within 30 days", "Use for at least five years"],
 "Under Re Ellenborough Park an easement needs a dominant and servient tenement, accommodation of the dominant land, different owners and a right capable of grant."),
("A neighbour has walked a path across land openly and without permission. What length of use can found prescription?",
 "20 years", ["12 years", "10 years", "40 years"],
 "Easements by prescription need 20 years' use as of right: without force, secrecy or permission."),
("A buyer's land carries an old covenant to maintain a boundary fence. Does it bind her?",
 "No, the burden does not run", ["Yes, all covenants pass", "Yes, if made by deed", "Only if she knew of it"],
 "The burden of a positive freehold covenant does not run with the land at law or in equity (Rhone v Stephens), so a later owner is not bound directly."),
("When does a restrictive covenant over registered land bind a buyer?",
 "If protected by a notice", ["Always, as it runs with land", "Only if the buyer agreed", "Only within 21 years"],
 "The burden runs in equity (Tulk v Moxhay) but for a registered disposition it binds a buyer only if protected by a notice on the register."),
("A lender sells a repossessed house. What duty does it owe the borrower on sale?",
 "To get the best price reasonably", ["To wait for the market to rise", "To sell at the original price", "To let the borrower pick"],
 "A mortgagee has no duty to delay sale but must take reasonable care to obtain the true market value or best price reasonably obtainable (Cuckmere Brick)."),
("A squatter has occupied registered land for ten years and applies to be registered. What happens next?",
 "The registered owner is notified", ["Squatter registered at once", "The title passes after 12 years", "The application is refused"],
 "Under Sch 6 LRA 2002, after ten years a squatter may apply; the registered proprietor is notified and can object, and usually defeats the claim by evicting within two years."),
("An agreement grants exclusive possession of a flat for a term at a rent, but it is called a licence. What is it?",
 "A lease", ["A licence", "An easement", "A profit"],
 "Under Street v Mountford exclusive possession for a term at a rent creates a lease, whatever label the parties use, unless an exception applies."),
("A post-1995 lease is lawfully assigned. What happens to the original tenant's liability?",
 "Released, subject to any AGA", ["Continues for the whole term", "Continues for six years", "Passes to the landlord"],
 "Under the Landlord and Tenant (Covenants) Act 1995 the tenant is released on a lawful assignment, but may have to give an authorised guarantee agreement for the assignee."),
("Two charges are registered against the same title. How is priority between them decided?",
 "By order of registration", ["By order of creation", "By the larger amount", "By the first lender's choice"],
 "Under s.48 LRA 2002 registered charges rank according to the order shown on the register, which follows the order of registration."),
]
